{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And your enemies shall fall before you by the sword.</b> First He promised (Leviticus 26:7) that they shall pursue their enemies and they shall fall by their sword, and He returned and repeated, \"and your enemies shall fall before you by the sword,\" meaning that He will grant them courage and might to pursue five hundred, and He will place faintness in the heart of the enemies so that a hundred flee from five and they all fall by the sword of the five. For it is possible that they will flee before them in terror, and the five will not be able to kill them by the sword because of their small number. And R. Abraham ibn Ezra said (ibn Ezra on Leviticus 26:8) that the repetition means that they will fall time after time, continuously, without recovery."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:00:40.547814680Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}